WHM (Web Host Manager) and cPanel are two interconnected tools widely used for web hosting management, 
especially in shared or reseller hosting environments. Here's a breakdown of what each does:
🔧 cPanel (Control Panel):
User-level web hosting control panel
Designed for website owners or end users
Provides a graphical interface to manage:
Domains and subdomains
Email accounts and forwarders
Files (using File Manager or FTP)
Databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL)
SSL certificates
Backups
Software installations (e.g., WordPress via Softaculous)
Easy to use even for non-technical users
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
🛠️ WHM (Web Host Manager):
Admin-level control panel
Used by resellers, system administrators, or web hosting providers
Used to manage:
Multiple cPanel accounts
Server-wide settings
Hosting packages (limits for cPanel accounts)
DNS zone files
Service monitoring (Apache, MySQL, etc.)
Security settings (firewalls, brute force protection)
SSL installations on multiple domains
Software updates
